Z||000000||BENGAL4||04-11-2000||06:32 PM||||Well, I dropped my 86GT off at the Fiero Shop in Toronto. What a place. When you enter the parking lot, all you see are Fieros. The first thing you notice in the showroom is a drag Fiero coupe. I was in heaven. Joe and Miriame, the owners, are super people. They showed me around and I noticed 2 3800 S/C and a Northstar on cradles ready for installation. My engine will arrive there next Tuesday or Wednesday. I found a 1997 3800 II S/C, with 8,000 miles, in Cincinnati. The engine cost me $1500.00. It is complete with harness, ECM, everything I need for the swap.<P>Miriame said they would take pics of the whole process, so I will post when I get them. It should take about 6 to 8 weeks to complete. I CANT WAIT. ||||reg||10
